# Bangladesh Grid Explorer

Spent the past few hours turning Bangladesh's daily power grid reports into something people can actually explore.

PGCB publishes a daily report on the national grid. All real, all public.

So I built a small site around it.

The site lets you explore:

* Today's demand vs. generation
* Hour-by-hour load-shedding
* All tracked power plants and why any are offline
* Peak load and fuel mix by zone
* Every substation's load across the country, including voltage
* A rough CO₂ estimate for the day

It's **free, open, and updates whenever a new day's report is added.**

Right now, you can track the data back to **July 2025**. When I get some free time, I'd like to see if I can work backward all the way to **2020** and turn this into a much longer historical record of Bangladesh's grid.

I'm an electrical engineer, not a web designer. I handled the data work, analysis, structure, and what I wanted the site to actually show. But I leaned heavily on Claude for the frontend coding and implementation.

So, a little credit to me, a lot of help from Claude, and hopefully some credit to the public data that made the whole thing possible.

Honestly, it was just fun to build.

I wanted to see the grid the way NLDC sees it, without having to open a spreadsheet.

And this is probably just the beginning.

Longer term, I'd love to take this toward a **real digital twin of the power system** — a live map of individual power plants and substations, not just zones, moving as the grid actually moves.

